-- CK-161: an unannotated function's dot-call `x.compare` never reaches a
-- derived `compare`. `Colour` has no `pub compare`, so its `compare` is
-- derived, which only an operator (`Red < Blue`) or a `where` clause
-- reaches: static-dispatch-spike.md §1.3 rule 2 and A.56, which the owner's
-- adoption of static dispatch (2026-09-18) took with it. `before`'s
-- promoted requirement keeps its dot-call's kind, so `before Red Blue` is
-- refused. Written red on 8b98464 expecting acceptance (rule 7: nothing is
-- guarded); acceptance reverses that rule, so it is the owner's decision
-- (plans/checker-findings.md CK-161). Until it is taken, R15-fix-E keeps
-- the refusal and fixes its message, which said only "no method called
-- `compare`": it now says why, and what to write — `x < y`, or a `where`
-- annotation, whose twin builds and prints `T`.
type Colour
    = Red
    | Blue


before x y =
    x.compare y == LT


result : Bool
result =
    before Red Blue
